                "Five things protect profits in this group. The grid grades each company on each; how each business works is explained in Tab 2. The short version: the strongest moats here are approvals and long contracts (Ellenbarrie's take-or-pay plants, Privi's contracts with fragrance houses, Premier's sole-source defence products), not chemistry. The weakest companies are those buying the same raw material as everyone else and selling at spot prices.",
